# Text style overrides

Change the text style of a single card only when the default does not work for it. Most cards need no override.

Home Assistant has no text style classes. You can change text in 2 ways:

- for all text, use the font size scale in the theme
- for one card, add a style with card-mod

## Make all text bigger

To make text bigger on every dashboard, raise Home Assistant's font size scale, `--ha-font-size-scale`. Every Civica size is multiplied by it, so the whole type scale grows together. Do not raise the size in each card instead.

## Change one card with card-mod

card-mod is a separate custom integration. Some Civica cards, such as the action buttons, already need it. Add a `card_mod` style to the card, and change only the property you need.

This example is a Markdown card for an invented household's energy summary. It lines up the digits and lets a long device name wrap.

```yaml
type: markdown
content: |
  **Today**

  - Solar: 12.4 kWh
  - Grid import: 3.1 kWh
  - Upstairs landing dehumidifier by the airing cupboard: 0.8 kWh
card_mod:
  style: |
    ha-card {
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
```

A Markdown card on its own can add headings, lists and bold text. It cannot change the text size. Do not use a heading to make text bigger: [Headings](typography-headings.html#a-reading-is-not-a-heading) explains why.

## What you can change

| To | Use | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Align text | `text-align: start` or `center` | Left-align most text. Centre only a short line, such as a reading in a gauge. Do not justify text. |
| Change the size | `font-size: var(--civica-font-size-body)` | Use a variable from the [type scale](typography-type-scale.html), never a fixed px size. |
| Change the weight | `font-weight: 400` or `700` | Use only regular and bold. |
| Line up numbers | `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` | Every digit has the same width, so readings in a column line up and a changing number does not jump. |
| Break long words | `overflow-wrap: anywhere` | A long name or address wraps instead of spilling out of the card. Civica cards already do this. |

Use `text-align: start`, not `left`. Then text in a right-to-left language aligns to the right edge.

Use overrides sparingly. Each one makes a card look different from the rest of the dashboard.
